# Personal notification credentials — copy to .env for local runs.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored. In GitHub Actions these belong in repository secrets
# (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions), which are NOT copied into a
# fork: everyone connects their own channel.
#
# All values are optional. Without them the site, the calendar feeds and the
# daily refresh work exactly the same — only the messages stay silent, and
# `npm run remind` prints what it *would* send.
#
# A webhook URL is a password: anyone holding it can post into your space.
# Never commit it, and never paste it into an issue or a pull request.

# --- Google Chat (incoming webhook) -----------------------------------------
# Google Chat > your space > Apps & integrations > Webhooks > Add webhook > copy URL
# Prefer a different secret name on GitHub? Keep your secret and set the
# repository variable GOOGLE_CHAT_SECRET_NAME to its name. See docs/setup-google-chat.md
GOOGLE_CHAT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- Email (SMTP) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Gmail: use an App Password with smtp.gmail.com:587
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
REMINDER_EMAIL_TO=
REMINDER_EMAIL_FROM=
